{
  "description": "R10: every non-built-in adapter's switch toggles off from the keyboard and is written to plugins-state.json, stays off across a restart, and toggling back on survives a restart too",
  "requirement": "R10 (GPUI Phase 1)",
  "notes": [
    "Adapters are fixtures/adapters.json (ubilink-core's defaults, cross-checked by fixtures --check). The 8 non-built-in ones are toggled; Finder and Safari are built-in and must stay on.",
    "Each Switch's accessible name is the adapter's app name exactly (README contract). It is reached with Tab (key_until, U4) and toggled with Space.",
    "plugins-state.json is ubilink-app's format ({\"disabled\": [lowercased app names]}, app/src/state.rs), in the instance's data dir."
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "name": "open settings",
      "call": "trigger_hotkey",
      "args": {
        "action": "settings"
      },
      "expect": {
        "shell.visible": true,
        "route": "settings"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "every adapter has a switch, all on",
      "see": [
        {
          "role": "Switch",
          "text": "Arc",
          "exact": true,
          "state": {
            "toggled": true
          }
        },
        {
          "role": "Switch",
          "text": "Bear",
          "exact": true,
          "state": {
            "toggled": true
          }
        },
        {
